  "cap_selection_rationale": [
    "The uncapped pool contains 41,466,136 bytes, but llama.cpp alone contributes 59.5% and C++ alone contributes 40.3%.",
    "A 128 KiB file cap removes only the largest 47 of 3,389 accepted files while excluding 11.7 MB concentrated in unusually large translation units and headers.",
    "A 5 MB repository cap prevents either llama.cpp or the MCP TypeScript SDK from dominating while retaining all five smaller repositories.",
    "A 30% per-language cap preserves both indentation-sensitive and brace-delimited code; the selected pool's largest language remains below 30%.",
    "The 7,500-occurrence identifier cap sits below source-specific concentrations such as ggml_tensor (9,889 uncapped) without treating language keywords as identifiers.",
    "Four files per SimHash cluster suppresses repeated templates while tolerating the audit's deliberately approximate cross-language near-duplicate detector.",
    "The strict scenario produced only 13,057,321 bytes and cannot fill the 16 MB C8 code allocation. The balanced scenario produced 16,159,545 bytes; the permissive scenario reached 17 MB but retained materially more repository and duplicate concentration."
  ],
